% External Infusion Pumps: LCD L33794 and its Policy Article A52507 (DME
% MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states
% when a claim for an external infusion pump, the drug it administers or its
% supplies is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY, for three of the LCD's indications:
%   IV, continuous subcutaneous insulin — the insulin pump E0784 for
%   diabetes (the Article's ICD-10 group 1), criterion A (the C-peptide
%   test: at most 110 percent of the lower limit of normal, or 200 percent
%   with a creatinine clearance of at most 50 ml/minute, with a fasting
%   blood sugar of at most 225 mg/dl at the same time) or B (a positive
%   beta cell autoantibody test), and criterion C (a comprehensive diabetes
%   education program, at least six months of multiple daily injections —
%   at least 3 a day — with frequent self-adjustments of the dose, glucose
%   self-testing at least 4 times a day in the two months before the pump,
%   and one of the clinical criteria 1-5) or D (on a pump before Medicare
%   enrollment, testing at least 4 times a day in the month before); the
%   Article's reading that a documented continuous glucose monitor meets the
%   testing requirement; the pump ordered and followed by a practitioner
%   managing multiple beneficiaries on insulin infusion with a team; and
%   continued coverage with an evaluation by the treating practitioner at
%   least every three months. The insulin (J1811, J1813, J1817) and the
%   insulin pump supplies (A4224, A4225) are covered with a covered pump;
%   the non-insulin supplies (A4221, A4222, K0552) never with E0784;
%   V(E), epoprostenol (J1325) or treprostinil (J3285) for pulmonary
%   hypertension with the pump K0455 only — the disease criteria (not
%   secondary to pulmonary venous hypertension or a respiratory disorder;
%   primary, or secondary to a listed condition; progressed despite maximal
%   treatment; a mean pulmonary artery pressure above 25 mm Hg at rest or 30
%   with exertion; significant symptoms; calcium channel blockers tried and
%   failed or ruled out); a backup pump is not separately payable;
%   V(H), subcutaneous immune globulin (J1551, J1555, J1558, J1559, J1561,
%   J1569, J1575) with the pump the Article's table pairs it with (E0779,
%   E0781) — administered in the home, the practitioner's determination
%   that home administration is necessary and appropriate, and a primary
%   immune deficiency (ICD-10 group 3) or a chronic inflammatory
%   demyelinating polyneuropathy (group 6) that responded to intravenous
%   immune globulin.
% The drug necessitating a covered pump and the supplies of a covered pump
% are covered with it ("When an infusion pump is covered, the drug
% necessitating the use of the pump and necessary supplies are also
% covered"); a drug alone is not. The benefit is durable medical equipment
% (Policy Article A52507), used in a home (dmepos.le); the disposable drug
% delivery systems (A4305, A4306, A9274) are in scope and in no benefit.
% The payment condition the policy adds (section remedy): the dispensing cap
% of the LCD's refill paragraph, a three-month quantity of a drug or supply
% at a time (a pump is not dispensed).
%
% ICD-10 table. The Article's table (sources/icd10/A52507_icd10_covered.csv,
% 460 rows, loaded as the table infusion_icd10) has six groups; the
% Article's text file does not carry the "Group N" paragraphs, so they are
% mapped to codes from the LCD's cross-references and the rows' contents:
%   group 1 — diabetes mellitus (E08-E13): the insulin pump E0784, its
%             insulin and supplies (read);
%   group 2 — hypercalcemia (E83.52): gallium nitrate (not modelled);
%   group 3 — primary immune deficiencies (D80-D83, G11.3): subcutaneous
%             immune globulin, criterion 4 (read);
%   group 4 — Parkinson's disease (G20.A1-G20.B2): the infusion therapies
%             for Parkinson's disease, J7340 and J7356 (not modelled);
%   group 5 — acute lymphoblastic leukemia (C91.0x): blinatumomab J9039
%             (not modelled);
%   group 6 — chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuritis (G61.81):
%             subcutaneous immune globulin, criterion 5 (read).
%
% How the criteria are read. What the record states is a scenario fact: the
% laboratory values as numbers (the C-peptide level as a percent of the
% laboratory's lower limit of normal — "connecting peptide" in the
% templates, a capital C alone reading as a variable; the fasting blood
% sugar; the creatinine clearance; the glycosylated hemoglobin), the
% injections a day and the months of the regimen, the average self-tests a
% day, the documented conditions (the shared template "the medical record
% of B documents C": the clinical criteria 1-5, continuous glucose monitor
% use), the practitioner's evaluations (dated, in the words of
% support_surfaces.le), the pressures (in the words of nebulizers.le), the
% drug a pump administers (in the words of nebulizers.le) and the supplies
% it is used with (the shared accessory template). That a subcutaneous
% immune globulin is an FDA-approved pooled plasma derivative labeled for
% subcutaneous use is carried by its HCPCS code. Therapy with a pump starts
% on its delivery; three months are read as 91 days. The findings this
% policy reads (the judged template of dmepos.le), and the criterion each
% stands for:
%   frequent insulin dose self adjustment (criterion C: "with frequent
%   self-adjustments of insulin dose");
%   qualifying pulmonary hypertension etiology, pulmonary hypertension
%   progressed despite treatment, significant pulmonary hypertension
%   symptoms, calcium channel blockers excluded (V(E), the disease criteria
%   — the names nebulizers.le reads for the same criteria of inhaled
%   treprostinil);
%   home immune globulin administration appropriate (V(H) criterion 3: "The
%   treating practitioner has determined that administration of the SCIg in
%   the patient's home is medically necessary and appropriate").
%
% Left out (the LCD's other indications, each a program of its own size):
% I deferoxamine, II chemotherapy for hepatocellular or colorectal cancer,
% III morphine for cancer pain, V(A) the anticancer drugs by continuous
% infusion, V(B) narcotic analgesics, V(C) the antifungal and antiviral
% drugs, V(D) the inotropic drugs for Stage D or Class IV heart failure,
% V(F) gallium nitrate, V(G) ziconotide, V(I) the Parkinson's disease
% infusions, V(J) blinatumomab — and with them the pumps E0780 and E0791,
% which only those indications use, the criteria sets (1) and (2), the
% heparin exclusion, the IV pole E0776 and the infusion controller E1399.
% Not modelled either: the insulin pumps with an integrated continuous
% glucose monitor (E0784 with E2102 or E2103: the Glucose Monitors LCD),
% the maintenance supplies' "not to exceed 4 weeks per episode" between
% periods of use, the cassettes per dose, drug wastage and the JB, JK, JL,
% JW, JZ, KX, GA, GY and GZ modifiers, the batteries, the dispensing
% entity's licensing, compounded drugs (J7999, Q9977). J1561 and J1569 are
% also intravenous immune globulin codes (ivig.le): in a model holding both
% policies such a claim meets both.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record: the pump and its drug — in the words of nebulizers.le and
    % support_surfaces.le (candidates for dmepos.le)
    *a drug* is administered with *a device*; undefined.
    the treating practitioner evaluated *a beneficiary* for *an item* on *a date*; undefined.
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of *a beneficiary* at rest is *a number* mm Hg; undefined.
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of *a beneficiary* with exertion is *a number* mm Hg; undefined.
    % the record: the insulin pump criteria
    the connecting peptide level of *a beneficiary* is *a number* percent of the lower limit of normal; undefined.
    the fasting blood sugar of *a beneficiary* at the connecting peptide test is *a number* mg per dl; undefined.
    the creatinine clearance of *a beneficiary* is *a number* ml per minute; undefined.
    the beta cell autoantibody test of *a beneficiary* is positive; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has completed a comprehensive diabetes education program; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* took *a number* insulin injections per day for *a second number* months before the insulin pump; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* self tested glucose an average of *a number* times per day during the two months before the insulin pump; undefined.
    the glycosylated hemoglobin of *a beneficiary* on multiple injections is *a number* percent; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* was on an external insulin infusion pump before enrollment in Medicare; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* self tested glucose an average of *a number* times per day during the month before enrollment in Medicare; undefined.
    the insulin pump of *a beneficiary* is ordered by a practitioner managing multiple beneficiaries on continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion with a knowledgeable team; undefined.
    % the record: the other pumps
    *an item* is a backup pump; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* receives the immune globulin in the home; undefined.
    the chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy of *a beneficiary* responded to intravenous immune globulin; undefined.
    % the tables
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table infusion_icd10.
    immune globulin code *a code* is used with pump *an other code* under table scig_pumps.
    % derived
    the diagnosis of *a beneficiary* is in infusion pump ICD10 group *a group*.
    *a device* is a covered insulin pump on the date of service of *a claim*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the insulin pump criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the insulin deficiency criterion.
    *a beneficiary* meets the insulin regimen criterion.
    the glucose self testing of *a beneficiary* before the insulin pump is sufficient.
    the glucose self testing of *a beneficiary* before enrollment is sufficient.
    *a beneficiary* meets an insulin pump clinical criterion.
    *a condition* is an insulin pump clinical criterion.
    the follow up of *a device* is current on the date of service of *a claim*.
    *a device* administers a covered infusion drug.
    *a drug* is a covered infusion drug for *a device*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the pulmonary hypertension infusion criteria.
    the pulmonary artery pressure of *a beneficiary* meets the infusion criterion.
    *a beneficiary* meets the subcutaneous immune globulin criteria.
    *a beneficiary* has a subcutaneous immune globulin diagnosis.
    *a claim* is within the dispensing limit for infusion drugs and supplies.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table: the diagnoses of the six groups (the
% header lists which are read).
the table infusion_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52507_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

% The Article's table of the pumps each subcutaneous immune globulin is
% administered with.
the table scig_pumps is, with all matches, with provenance Policy Article A52507,
        confer "Specific infusion pump HCPCS codes are used with specific SCIg preparations according to the table below":
    drug | pump | confer
    "J1555" or "J1559" or "J1561" or "J1569" | "E0779" | "Infusion Pump SCIg Preparation E0779 J1555, J1559, J1561, J1569"
    "J1575" | "E0781" | "E0781 J1575"
    "J1551" or "J1558" | "E0779" | "E0779 or E0781 J1551, J1558"
    "J1551" or "J1558" | "E0781" | "E0779 or E0781 J1551, J1558"

the knowledge base external_infusion_pumps includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base external_infusion_pumps includes:

LCD L33794 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33794".
the text of LCD L33794 is at "sources/lcd/L33794.txt".
Policy Article A52507 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52507".
the text of Policy Article A52507 is at "sources/article/A52507.txt".

% The diagnosis of the claim, read against the Article's table.
rule infusion_diagnosis_group with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Refer to the ICD-10 code list in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses.":
the diagnosis of a beneficiary is in infusion pump ICD10 group a group
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A52507" as a description under table infusion_icd10.

% The clinical criteria 1-5 of criterion C other than the glycosylated
% hemoglobin, as documented conditions.
history of recurring hypoglycemia is an insulin pump clinical criterion,
    as stated in LCD L33794, confer "History of recurring hypoglycemia".
wide fluctuations in blood glucose before mealtime is an insulin pump clinical criterion,
    as stated in LCD L33794, confer "Wide fluctuations in blood glucose before mealtime".
dawn phenomenon with frequently high fasting blood sugars is an insulin pump clinical criterion,
    as stated in LCD L33794, confer "Dawn phenomenon with fasting blood sugars frequently exceeding 200 mg/dL".
history of severe glycemic excursions is an insulin pump clinical criterion,
    as stated in LCD L33794, confer "History of severe glycemic excursions".

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides — the pumps, drugs and supplies of the
% modelled indications, and the disposable systems — and their benefit:
% durable medical equipment (Policy Article A52507), but not the
% disposable drug delivery systems.
rule infusion_codes with provenance Policy Article A52507,
        confer "External infusion pumps are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(6))":
the policy for code a code is external_infusion_pumps
    if the code is in ["E0779", "E0781", "E0784", "K0455", "A4221", "A4222", "K0552", "A4224", "A4225", "J1811", "J1813", "J1817", "J1325", "J3285", "J1551", "J1555", "J1558", "J1559", "J1561", "J1569", "J1575", "A4305", "A4306", "A9274"].

section applicability is:

% "Disposable drug delivery systems, including elastomeric infusion pumps
% (A4305, A4306, A9274) are non-covered devices because they do not meet the
% Medicare definition of durable medical equipment."
rule infusion_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52507,
        confer "External infusion pumps are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(6))":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is external_infusion_pumps
    and it is not the case that
        the code is in ["A4305", "A4306", "A9274"].

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Indication IV: the insulin pump, its insulin and its supplies.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule infusion_insulin_pump_claim with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Subcutaneous insulin is administered using ambulatory infusion pump E0784. Claims for usage of infusion pumps other than E0784 will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a covered insulin pump on the date of service of the claim.

rule infusion_insulin_claim with provenance Policy Article A52507,
        confer "Use code J1811, J1813 or J1817 for insulin administered through an external insulin pump (E0784)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J1811", "J1813", "J1817"]
    and the item is administered with a device
    and the device is a covered insulin pump on the date of service of the claim.

rule infusion_insulin_supplies_claim with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Supplies for the maintenance of a parenteral drug infusion catheter (A4221) or supplies for the maintenance for an insulin infusion pump (A4224) are covered during the period of covered use of an infusion pump":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4224", "A4225"]
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a covered insulin pump on the date of service of the claim.

% the pump E0784, for a beneficiary meeting the criteria, followed up
rule infusion_insulin_pump_covered with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Administration of continuous subcutaneous insulin for the treatment of diabetes mellitus (Refer to the ICD-10 code list in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses.) if criterion A or B is met and if criterion C or D is met":
a device is a covered insulin pump on the date of service of a claim
    if the HCPCS code of the device is "E0784"
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the insulin pump criteria
    and the follow up of the device is current on the date of service of the claim.

rule infusion_insulin_criteria with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "In addition, the external insulin infusion pump must be ordered and follow-up care rendered by a practitioner who manages multiple beneficiaries on continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion therapy and who works closely with a team including nurses, diabetic educators, and dieticians who are knowledgeable in the use of continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion therapy":
a beneficiary meets the insulin pump criteria
    if the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in infusion pump ICD10 group 1
    and the beneficiary meets the insulin deficiency criterion
    and the beneficiary meets the insulin regimen criterion
    and the insulin pump of the beneficiary is ordered by a practitioner managing multiple beneficiaries on continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion with a knowledgeable team.

% Criterion A, alternatives 1 and 2, each with 3.
rule infusion_criterion_a1 with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "C-peptide level is less than or equal to 110 percent of the lower limit of normal of the laboratory's measurement method":
a beneficiary meets the insulin deficiency criterion
    if the connecting peptide level of the beneficiary is a number percent of the lower limit of normal
    and the number <= 110
    and the fasting blood sugar of the beneficiary at the connecting peptide test is an other number mg per dl
    and the other number <= 225.

rule infusion_criterion_a2 with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "a fasting C-peptide level is less than or equal to 200 per cent of the lower limit of normal":
a beneficiary meets the insulin deficiency criterion
    if the creatinine clearance of the beneficiary is a number ml per minute
    and the number <= 50
    and the connecting peptide level of the beneficiary is an other number percent of the lower limit of normal
    and the other number <= 200
    and the fasting blood sugar of the beneficiary at the connecting peptide test is a third number mg per dl
    and the third number <= 225.

% (criterion 3 in both rules: "A fasting blood sugar obtained at the same
% time as the C-peptide level is less than or equal to 225 mg/dl")

% Criterion B.
rule infusion_criterion_b with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Beta cell autoantibody test is positive":
a beneficiary meets the insulin deficiency criterion
    if the beta cell autoantibody test of the beneficiary is positive.

% Criterion C: education, six months of at least 3 injections a day with
% frequent self-adjustment, the testing, one of the clinical criteria.
rule infusion_criterion_c with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "The beneficiary has completed a comprehensive diabetes education program, has been on a program of multiple daily injections of insulin (i.e., at least 3 injections per day) with frequent self-adjustments of insulin dose for at least 6 months prior to initiation of the insulin pump":
a beneficiary meets the insulin regimen criterion
    if the beneficiary has completed a comprehensive diabetes education program
    and the beneficiary took a number insulin injections per day for an other number months before the insulin pump
    and the number >= 3
    and the other number >= 6
    and the finding frequent insulin dose self adjustment about the beneficiary is established
    and the glucose self testing of the beneficiary before the insulin pump is sufficient
    and the beneficiary meets an insulin pump clinical criterion.

% Criterion D.
rule infusion_criterion_d with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "The beneficiary has been on an external insulin infusion pump prior to enrollment in Medicare and has documented frequency of glucose self-testing an average of at least 4 times per day during the month prior to Medicare enrollment":
a beneficiary meets the insulin regimen criterion
    if the beneficiary was on an external insulin infusion pump before enrollment in Medicare
    and the glucose self testing of the beneficiary before enrollment is sufficient.

% The testing: an average of at least 4 a day, or a continuous glucose
% monitor documented (the Article).
rule infusion_testing_before_pump with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "has documented frequency of glucose self-testing an average of at least 4 times per day during the 2 months prior to initiation of the insulin pump":
the glucose self testing of a beneficiary before the insulin pump is sufficient
    if the beneficiary self tested glucose an average of a number times per day during the two months before the insulin pump
    and the number >= 4.

rule infusion_testing_cgm_before_pump with provenance Policy Article A52507,
        confer "Documentation of the use of a CGM device in the beneficiary’s medical records would meet the testing requirement in the External Infusion Pump LCD":
the glucose self testing of a beneficiary before the insulin pump is sufficient
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents continuous glucose monitor use.

rule infusion_testing_before_enrollment with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "has documented frequency of glucose self-testing an average of at least 4 times per day during the month prior to Medicare enrollment":
the glucose self testing of a beneficiary before enrollment is sufficient
    if the beneficiary self tested glucose an average of a number times per day during the month before enrollment in Medicare
    and the number >= 4.

rule infusion_testing_cgm_before_enrollment with provenance Policy Article A52507,
        confer "Documentation of the use of a CGM device in the beneficiary’s medical records would meet the testing requirement in the External Infusion Pump LCD":
the glucose self testing of a beneficiary before enrollment is sufficient
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents continuous glucose monitor use.

% The clinical criteria 1-5 while on multiple injections.
rule infusion_clinical_hba1c with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Glycosylated hemoglobin level (HbA1C) greater than 7 percent":
a beneficiary meets an insulin pump clinical criterion
    if the glycosylated hemoglobin of the beneficiary on multiple injections is a number percent
    and the number > 7.

rule infusion_clinical_documented with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "meets one or more of the following criteria (1 - 5) while on the multiple injection regimen":
a beneficiary meets an insulin pump clinical criterion
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is an insulin pump clinical criterion.

% Continued coverage: the first three months (91 days) from the delivery of
% the pump need nothing more; afterwards an evaluation by the treating
% practitioner within the three months before the date of service.
rule infusion_follow_up_initial with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Continued coverage of an external insulin pump and supplies requires that the beneficiary be seen and evaluated by the treating practitioner at least every 3 months":
the follow up of a device is current on the date of service of a claim
    if the device was delivered on a date
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 91.

rule infusion_follow_up_evaluation with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Continued coverage of an external insulin pump and supplies requires that the beneficiary be seen and evaluated by the treating practitioner at least every 3 months":
the follow up of a device is current on the date of service of a claim
    if the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and the treating practitioner evaluated the beneficiary for the device on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 91.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The other pumps: covered with the drug they administer; the drug and the
% supplies covered with a covered pump.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule infusion_pump_claim with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "An external infusion pump is covered for the following indications (I-V)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["K0455", "E0779", "E0781"]
    and the item administers a covered infusion drug
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a backup pump.

% (the backup pump: "A second pump provided as a backup will be denied as
% not separately payable")

rule infusion_drug_claim with provenance Policy Article A52507,
        confer "Drugs are only covered as a supply to a covered DME infusion pump":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is administered with a device
    and the item is a covered infusion drug for the device.

rule infusion_non_insulin_supplies_claim with provenance Policy Article A52507,
        confer "Claims for codes A4221, A4222 and K0552 must only be used with a non-insulin external infusion pump (E0779, E0780, E0781, E0791 or K0455)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4221", "A4222", "K0552"]
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the HCPCS code of the device is an other code
    and the other code is in ["K0455", "E0779", "E0781"]
    and the device administers a covered infusion drug.

rule infusion_pump_with_covered_drug with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "When an infusion pump is covered, the drug necessitating the use of the pump and necessary supplies are also covered":
a device administers a covered infusion drug
    if a drug is administered with the device
    and the drug is a covered infusion drug for the device.

% V(E): epoprostenol or treprostinil, with K0455 only.
rule infusion_epoprostenol_treprostinil with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Epoprostenol/treprostinil is administered using ambulatory infusion pump K0455. Claims for usage of infusion pumps other than K0455 will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a drug is a covered infusion drug for a device
    if the HCPCS code of the drug is a code
    and the code is in ["J1325", "J3285"]
    and the HCPCS code of the device is "K0455"
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the pulmonary hypertension infusion criteria.

rule infusion_pulmonary_hypertension_criteria with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Administration of epoprostenol (J1325) or treprostinil (J3285) for beneficiaries with pulmonary hypertension if they meet the following disease criteria":
a beneficiary meets the pulmonary hypertension infusion criteria
    if the finding qualifying pulmonary hypertension etiology about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding pulmonary hypertension progressed despite treatment about the beneficiary is established
    and the pulmonary artery pressure of the beneficiary meets the infusion criterion
    and the finding significant pulmonary hypertension symptoms about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding calcium channel blockers excluded about the beneficiary is established.

% (the findings: "The pulmonary hypertension is not secondary to pulmonary
% venous hypertension" and "The beneficiary has primary pulmonary
% hypertension or pulmonary hypertension, which is secondary to one of the
% following conditions"; "The pulmonary hypertension has progressed despite
% maximal medical and/or surgical treatment of the identified condition";
% "The beneficiary has significant symptoms from the pulmonary
% hypertension"; "Treatment with oral calcium channel blocking agents has
% been tried and failed, or has been considered and ruled out")

rule infusion_mpap_at_rest with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "The mean pulmonary artery pressure is greater than 25 mm Hg at rest or greater than 30 mm Hg with exertion":
the pulmonary artery pressure of a beneficiary meets the infusion criterion
    if the mean pulmonary artery pressure of the beneficiary at rest is a number mm Hg
    and the number > 25.

rule infusion_mpap_with_exertion with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "The mean pulmonary artery pressure is greater than 25 mm Hg at rest or greater than 30 mm Hg with exertion":
the pulmonary artery pressure of a beneficiary meets the infusion criterion
    if the mean pulmonary artery pressure of the beneficiary with exertion is a number mm Hg
    and the number > 30.

% V(H): subcutaneous immune globulin, with the pump of the Article's table.
rule infusion_scig with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "If a drug and pump combination is used, other than those listed in the table in the LCD-related Policy Article, the pump and drug will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a drug is a covered infusion drug for a device
    if the HCPCS code of the drug is a code
    and the HCPCS code of the device is an other code
    and immune globulin code the code is used with pump the other code under table scig_pumps
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the subcutaneous immune globulin criteria.

rule infusion_scig_criteria with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Subcutaneous immune globulin (SCIg) (see Group 3 HCPCS codes) is covered when criteria 1-3, AND criterion 4 or 5 are met":
a beneficiary meets the subcutaneous immune globulin criteria
    if the beneficiary receives the immune globulin in the home
    and the finding home immune globulin administration appropriate about the beneficiary is established
    and the beneficiary has a subcutaneous immune globulin diagnosis.

% (criterion 2: "The SCIg is administered in the home"; criterion 1, the
% FDA-approved pooled plasma derivative, is carried by the code)

rule infusion_scig_primary_immune_deficiency with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "The beneficiary has a primary immune deficiency disorder (Refer to the ICD-10 code list in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses.)":
a beneficiary has a subcutaneous immune globulin diagnosis
    if the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in infusion pump ICD10 group 3.

rule infusion_scig_cidp with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "The beneficiary has a diagnosis of chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy (CIDP) that has responded to IVIg treatment":
a beneficiary has a subcutaneous immune globulin diagnosis
    if the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in infusion pump ICD10 group 6
    and the chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy of the beneficiary responded to intravenous immune globulin.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own condition of payment: the dispensing cap of the LCD's
% refill paragraph for the drugs and supplies; a pump is not dispensed (a
% device of this model).
rule infusion_documentation with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Regardless of utilization, a supplier must not dispense more than a three (3) - month quantity at a time":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is external_infusion_pumps
    and the claim is within the dispensing limit for infusion drugs and supplies.

rule infusion_dispensing_supply with provenance LCD L33794,
        confer "Regardless of utilization, a supplier must not dispense more than a three (3) - month quantity at a time":
a claim is within the dispensing limit for infusion drugs and supplies
    if the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 3.

rule infusion_dispensing_pump:
a claim is within the dispensing limit for infusion drugs and supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0779", "E0781", "E0784", "K0455"].
